      "id": "G002",
      "gap": "Absence of principled, automated approaches for estimating data-dependent trimming parameters (alpha) and minimum membership thresholds (s) in relaxed robust clustering frameworks.",
      "why_it_matters": "Practitioners are currently forced to test parameters over an arbitrary range or rely on manual tuning, limiting the deployment of robust trimmed K-means variants in automated, large-scale pipelines.",
      "what_is_known": "Relaxed continuous simplex formulations and trimmed K-means models successfully identify outliers and multi-membership clusters when trimming proportions alpha and minimum cluster memberships s are specified.",
      "what_remains_unknown": "How to design fully automated, mathematically principled parameter selection mechanisms that estimate alpha and s dynamically during optimization.",
